<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslav Oct PPI up 1.5 pct, y/y falls to 68.0 pct.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav Oct PPI up 1.5 pct, y/y falls to 68.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistical Office reported the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV PRODUCER PRICES  OCT 96    SEPT 96	OCT 95</p>
<p> monthly PPI index change  +  1.5     +1.0	  n.a.</p>
<p> yr/yr change		  + 68.0    +79.2	  n.a.</p>
<p> Change vs avge 1995	 +104.1    +101.1     + 95</p>
<p>NOTES: Producer prices rose 40.7 percent in the January- October period. Cummulative January-September producer prices rose 99.5 percent against the same period last year, and 85.5 percent against the average for 1995.</p>
<p>Figures refer to rump Federal Republic of Yugoslavia, comprising Serbia and Montenegro.</p>
<p>-- Amra Kevic, Belgrade newsroom +381 11 2224305</p>
